STATUS: Generate one transparent sprite sheet containing the three campaign
level-number plaque backgrounds shown in the latest Chapter 1 campaign-map
screenshot. These are reusable UI assets; Android adds the level number and
status icons separately.

## Reference input

- Attach the campaign-map screenshot showing level 1 completed, level 2
  available, and the remaining levels locked. Use its three plaque treatments
  as the primary design reference.
- Match the screenshot's short, wide, beveled plaque shape and painterly
  fantasy materials. Keep the same silhouette, dimensions, camera angle,
  position, and border treatment for all three variants.
- The plaque is a separate overlay below a fortress or boss marker. Do not
  copy the map, marker illustration, progress bar, frame, or other UI.

## Output

- Generate exactly one PNG sprite sheet:
  `campaign_map_level_plates_sheet.png`.
- Save it under `assets_src/campaign/ui/`.
- Canvas: 3:1 landscape, RGBA. Prefer 1536 x 512 pixels. If the image
  generator uses a different fixed resolution, preserve the 3:1 aspect and
  three evenly spaced states.
- Arrange three equal-width cells horizontally, in this order:
  1. completed;
  2. available;
  3. locked.
- Center one plaque in each cell. Each plaque should occupy about 90% of its
  cell's width and 30% of its height, with identical bounds and alignment in
  all three cells. Keep the rest of the sheet genuinely transparent.
- Do not draw cell dividers, crop marks, labels, or a background. Do not
  generate separate files; the three cells will be extracted after review.

## Shared plaque shape

- Make each plaque a short, wide rectangular nameplate with restrained clipped
  corners, a beveled raised edge, and a shallow dark inset for the live level
  number.
- Keep all three shapes visually identical so the plaque does not jump or
  change size when a level changes state.
- Make the empty center high-contrast and wide enough for a one- or two-digit
  number. Leave space at the right edge for a separately rendered status icon.
- Use a polished but worn Orc campaign-map finish: hammered metal edges,
  dark timber or leather structure, and restrained antique-gold trim.

## State treatments

- **Completed, first cell:** dark charcoal or blackened timber face with
  understated bronze/gold bevels. Keep it subdued and readable against the
  map. The green checkmark is separate UI and must not be baked into the art.
- **Available, second cell:** deep crimson/oxblood face with a brighter gold
  bevel and richer highlights, matching the active level plaque in the
  screenshot. The amber glow around the fortress is a separate UI effect.
- **Locked, third cell:** warm parchment or light tan face with a worn
  dark-brown/gold edge, matching the locked level plaques in the screenshot.
  The padlock is separate UI.
- Keep the differences limited to material, color, and restrained highlight
  intensity. Do not change the outline, proportions, position, or perspective.

## Separation from live UI

- These are plaque backgrounds only. Do not draw numbers, words, letters,
  checkmarks, locks, badges, glow, selection rings, level labels, or any other
  status symbol.
- Do not make the available plaque's red face a faction banner or team cue.
- Do not place the plaque inside a circle, shield, pin, medallion, or pedestal.
- Do not draw a fortress, boss, map, terrain, route, scenery, characters, or
  extra decorative objects around the plaques.
- Preserve clean alpha edges with no colored fringe or detached pixels.

## Extraction after review

- Split the sheet into three equal-width columns using its actual dimensions,
  preserving the left-to-right state order; do not assume fixed pixel
  boundaries if the generator changes resolution.
- Use each plaque's alpha bounds to trim its cell. Normalize all three crops
  to the same pixel dimensions and centered position, preserving transparent
  alpha and any small intentional detail on the plate edges.
- The extracted source assets will be named:
  `campaign_level_plate_completed.png`,
  `campaign_level_plate_available.png`, and
  `campaign_level_plate_locked.png`.
- Preview all three at campaign-map display size before importing them into
  Android drawable resources.

## Negative prompt

opaque background, colored background, checkerboard, cell dividers, crop
marks, labels, text, letters, digits, numbers, checkmark, padlock, badge,
round frame, circle, shield, pin, medallion, pedestal, selection ring, glow,
status icon, fortress, boss, character, map, landscape, terrain, path, water,
sky, vegetation, scenery, multiple plaques in one cell, different plaque
sizes, different silhouettes, changing perspective, extreme filigree,
fleur-de-lis, clean modern UI, flat vector style, blurry edges, colored fringe,
detached pixels, signature, logo, watermark

## Review checklist

- Confirm one transparent 3:1 RGBA sprite sheet with exactly three equal cells.
- Confirm each cell contains one plaque at the same size, position, and angle.
- Confirm the left-to-right order is completed, available, locked.
- Confirm the completed face is dark, available is crimson with gold trim, and
  locked is warm parchment; all numbers and status symbols remain absent.
- Confirm the transparent cells have clean edges and no matte or background.
- Confirm the plaque shape and contrast remain legible behind both one- and
  two-digit level numbers.
